 Completed the separate coherent milestone implementation code review, actual nonempty runner, API/module demonstration and exit assessment in [milestone 1.1 report](reports/phases/1/1.1.md), reviewed at published T-003 source `373203d6f41bee2229eed900b761de8669678e0b`. The runner passed 21 unit and 12 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, with no skips/warnings. Mixed-terminator/non-ASCII/BOM temporary-file API and real CLI returned three lines/four words with exact streams/status and unchanged bytes; BOM-only default versus retaining calls visibly produced zero/zero versus one/one. Source review found no milestone contract blocker and no required repair; TODO is None. Full runtime/platform matrix, complete CLI failure diagnostics, public guide/distribution and later phase capabilities remain unverified/planned in their owning tasks.
 
 T-002/T-003 separate closing commits were inspected and published before this review; provider readback confirms issues #3/#4 closed/completed with evidence, and T-001 #2 remains closed. Unique T-004 issue is #5 in native milestone #1. The report/evidence, initial T-004 checkbox and eligible milestone 1.1 parent close together; phase and unselected tasks remain unchecked. Publish/read back this task commit before closing issue #5, then validate all milestone-associated task issues and close/read back milestone #1. Stop on the incomplete phase branch, with main unchanged and no release or T-005 work.
+
+## T-005 completion evidence
+
+Continued exactly T-005 from published local trial checkpoint `4a9c0625aad481bbe46db25a945f5c9fad135716` on `trial/a017-failed-check`. Startup verified the selected local trial-delivery ref exactly matched HEAD, with no outstanding commit; retained the three unstaged CLI/unit/integration artifacts and existing task identity/evidence. T-004 closing result/report/evidence/initial checkbox composition was inspected and compliant. Accepted governing contracts and Ready adjacent reviews remain equivalent; only completion annotations differ from preparation. The continuation explicitly authorizes local trial delivery and relevant existing core/API regression repair; origin remains read-only and hosted writes are excluded.
+
+Retained named-file CLI error handling returns 1 for OSError subclasses and UnicodeDecodeError, identifies input/cause on stderr, emits no partial stdout and no traceback. Usage validation precedes acquisition and returns 2 for missing/extra inputs and unknown options. Concrete delegated artifact review additionally found argparse abbreviations accepting unknown `--keep`/`--keep-b`; disabling abbreviation repairs this R-008 violation. Help, full `--keep-bom`, option order and dash-prefixed named files remain supported; literal `-` remains a file.
+
+The required retained check reproduced 23 unit tests/44 assertion failures and 14 integration tests/21 failures, attributable to the disclosed counting wrapper's extra line and altered public signature. Authorized repair restores the explicit annotated `count_text(text, *, strip_bom=True)` and shared normalized counting without a phantom line. New direct text/file literal expectations cover empty, BOM-only, CRLF-only and trailing blank lines, preventing file/text equivalence from hiding shared incorrect results; file bytes remain unchanged. Existing comprehensive semantics, constructor, API signature/silence, strict decode and owned-handle checks remain intact.
+
+On Python 3.12.14, with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` and `python -B` (inherited by child processes), the focused core/file/signature command `python -B -m unittest tests.unit.test_core.CountingTests.test_empty_and_terminated_input_have_no_phantom_line tests.integration.test_api.FileApiTests.test_file_counts_match_literal_boundary_expectations tests.integration.test_api.TextApiTests.test_signatures_and_keyword_only_policy -v` failed before core repair with three tests/nine failures, then passed all three. The focused prefix command `python -B -m unittest tests.unit.test_cli.CliTests.test_usage_failures_validate_before_acquisition tests.integration.test_cli.ModuleCliTests.test_unknown_option_is_usage_failure -v` failed before parser repair with two tests/four failures, then passed both. Unit prefix cases prove no acquisition; subprocess cases prove status 2 rather than missing-file status 1. The original interrupted CLI's earlier focused RED/GREEN is retained as prior evidence; no reset or invented chronology was used.
+
+Final `python -B tools/check_tests.py` returned 0 with 24 independently discovered unit and 15 integration tests passing, no skips or warnings. Coverage includes controlled missing/unreadable/read/decode exceptions, actual missing/bad-byte subprocesses, status/output/diagnostics, help/success/BOM/dash-name regressions, complete counting/public API/resource behavior, unchanged bytes and runner nonempty/failure propagation. `git diff --check` is clean. CLI/core docstrings accurately describe current contracts. Public guide, README/distribution expansion, JSON/stdin/range and other runtimes remain outside this task.
+
+The coordinator accepted the exact six-file corrected implementation/test artifacts before task closure; published decision `2d48e1cee34676556a624f7602861b070e135a7a` retains the original prefix-status-0 probe and the separate counting/API repair assessment. Exactly T-005's result/tests/docstrings, current evidence and initial checkbox close together; no parent status or other task changes occur. Push and exact readback of the local trial ref immediately follow commit inspection. Stop before T-006, parent/phase closure and integration; origin and historical evidence remain unchanged.
